course: dictionary
lesson: 9303
title: Species: one word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Species is a word with two meanings, and the sentences around it tell you which one you need. In science, a species is a group of living things that are alike and can breed together to have young that can also have young. «A chihuahua and a Great Dane are the same species and could in theory have puppies together.» Even though they look very different, they belong to one species.
explain: In everyday talk, species can mean just a kind or sort. «The zoo has 12 species of monkey» means the zoo has twelve different kinds of monkey. The word is about counting kinds, not about breeding. Ask yourself: would kind fit here? If it does, you have the everyday meaning.
explain: Species is the same word for one and for many: one species, two species. «Lions are one species, tigers another» tells you that lions and tigers are different groups of animals. When you see species, check the context before you decide what it means.
fact: Species is a noun, and it is the same in the singular and the plural: a species, two species.
fact: «Species» means a group of living things that are alike and can breed together to have young that can also have young.
fact: «Species» can also mean a kind or sort, as in «twelve species of monkey».
fact: «Endangered» species are at risk of dying out; «extinct» species are gone for good.
fact: «Whaling» nearly wiped out some species; most whaling was banned in 1986, and humpbacks have recovered a lot.
exercise: «Lions are one species, tigers another.» What does species mean here? | A place where animals are kept | A loud noise | *A group of living things that are alike and can breed together | A type of food
exercise: «The zoo has 12 species of monkey.» Which meaning fits best? | *A kind or sort | A zookeeper | A group that can breed together only | Twelve monkeys in one cage
exercise: «Endangered species are at risk of dying out.» What does endangered mean? | Found only in the sea | Safe inside a zoo | *At risk of dying out | Very large and strong
test: «A chihuahua and a Great Dane are the same species and could in theory have puppies together.» Why are they one species? | They live in the same place | They are both very old | They have the same size | *They can breed together and have young that can also have young
test: Which word means a species that has died out completely? | humpback | habitat | *extinct | endangered
exam: In which sentence does species mean a kind or sort? | «A chihuahua and a Great Dane are the same species.» | *«The café sells twelve species of tea.» | «Whaling nearly wiped out some species.» | «Scientists map where each species lives.»
